The second line is part of the map, not an arbitrary completion of a partial section. Powers Mkn below
mean repeated feedback under (1), not composition powers of the original f .
    The first line chooses the least member of each kernel class. Least kernel transversals and inverse
matchings in transformation semigroups are established background [3, 5]. Indeed, f ◦ Mn (f ) ◦ f = f ,
and ef = Mn (f ) ◦ f is the idempotent retraction sending each position to the least member of its
ker f block. This does not make Mn a mutual inverse selection: for f = (0, 0), M2 (f ) = id but
M2 (f ) ◦ f ◦ M2 (f ) = f ̸= M2 (f ). The identity-on-missing rule is what controls subsequent path
splitting.
    First-occurrence encodings and their set-partition interpretation are also classical [2], as are functional-
digraph decomposition [4] and periodic-point zeta functions [1]. These ingredients, involution and Bell
numbers, and labelled-set calculus receive no contribution credit. The result proved here is only the exact
conjunction forced by the literal rule (1). No novelty or priority conclusion is drawn from the bounded
owner search.
    For x ∈ Xn , let tail(x) be its least entrance time into the recurrent set and let per(x) be its eventual
period. Write Yn = Mn (Xn ), let Rn be the number of recurrent points, and let In be the number of
