Theorem 1 (complete dynamics and one-step fibres). For the literal map (1), the following hold.
   (i) Every component of every g ∈ Yn is either a directed cycle or a loop-rooted directed path. One
       update inverts each cycle. If a path of size s > 1 in root-to-leaf order is P = (p0 , . . . , ps−1 ), one
       update reverses P when p0 > p1 , and otherwise splits off p0 and reverses the remaining path; a
       singleton is fixed. For n ≥ 2,
