                                    s≥1

which is (6).
   Every nonsingleton recurrent path is exchanged with its distinct reversal. Cycle inversion fixes exactly
the two-cycles. Thus a fixed state is a set of singleton loops and disjoint two-cycles, equivalently an
involution, and (2) applies. Every recurrent point has period one or two, while any point fixed by a
positive iterate is recurrent. This proves (7). Substitution into the Artin–Mazur definition
